-- Step 24: purchase orders and goods received.
-- track: B
--
-- The CREATE TABLE / index statements are generated by drizzle-kit from
-- src/modules/*/schema.ts. The sections marked "hand-written" are not managed by Drizzle.
-- Reverse with the file of the same name in drizzle/down.
--
-- A purchase order says what was ordered from a supplier, into which warehouse, at what cost
-- before tax. It is a draft the app writes; submitting it takes its PO number. Nothing reaches
-- the books or the stock with an order.
--
-- Goods received are written against one submitted order: how much of each of its lines
-- arrived, never more than is left of what was ordered. Posting them is one act of the
-- database: the goods go into the order's warehouse at the order's cost, and
--
--   debit   Stock in trade                    what the goods cost
--   credit  Goods received not invoiced       owed to the supplier, not yet billed
--
-- The supplier's bill (Step 25) will move the amount from Goods received not invoiced to Trade
-- payables. Until then, what that account holds is exactly the goods received and not billed.
--
-- The owner and an accountant write and submit orders. The warehouse receives goods: it writes
-- and posts goods received notes, in quantities only. It is not shown what an order costs: it
-- does not read the orders or their lines, and learns what is left to receive from
-- app.orders_to_receive and app.order_lines_to_receive, which give no cost. The app's role
-- cannot write a document's status, number, who did it, or its journal.
--
-- Database error codes of this track are SE200 to SE299 (docs/PARALLEL.md); Step 30 used SE200
-- to SE210:
--   SE211  no such purchase order or goods received note in this company (or outside the
--          member's branches)
--   SE212  the document is not in the state this needs
--   SE213  a submitted order or posted goods received note is never changed or removed
--   SE214  a line is written only while its document is a draft, and is a line of its order
--   SE215  an order is submitted with at least one line and a total that is its lines'
--   SE216  more goods received than is left of the order
--   SE217  goods received follow their order: its supplier, its warehouse, on or after its date
--   SE218  an order with goods received, or with a draft of goods received, is not cancelled
--   SE219  purchase documents are written in read committed transactions
--   SE220  a date that has not come yet, or is no day on the calendar
--   SE221  the supplier is archived
--   SE222  an item on the order is no longer ordered in the unit the order names

